{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2124","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2124","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2124\",\"parent_revision\":\"150b938118e8a0cc689450dfc77a3b44ea3c1ad1a4ea67ad303025a4c38803f4\",\"root_revision\":\"150b938118e8a0cc689450dfc77a3b44ea3c1ad1a4ea67ad303025a4c38803f4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA renamed or deleted plugin directory leaves a stale marketplace entry that passes lint but breaks installation for anyone using `marketplace.json` for discovery. Drift between `marketplace.json` `name` and plugin `plugin.json` `name` is also undetectable. Catching this only at install time means the bug ships to users.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Pattern observed in research/skill-generation-tools/waza.md \u2014 Waza's `./scripts/verify-skills.sh` enforces that \\\"every marketplace entry has a matching `skills/*/SKILL.md` directory\\\". The analogous check for this repo is plugin entry \u2192 plugin directory \u2192 matching plugin.json name.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **no validator detects stale plugin entries in marketplace.json** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from research/skill-generation-tools/waza.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` lists 30 plugin entries as `{ \\\"name\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"./plugins/...\\\" }`. There is no validator that walks each `source` path and confirms the referenced directory still exists with a valid `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, and that the `name` field in `marketplace.json` matches the `name` in the plugin's own `plugin.json`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` \u2014 30 plugin entries, no consistency check\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/auto_sync_manifests.py` \u2014 handles plugin component arrays and version fields, does not cross-reference marketplace entries\\n- `scripts/` \u2014 no `verify_marketplace_consistency.py` or equivalent\\n- Pre-commit config (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`) \u2014 no marketplace-consistency hook\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b68bf9764c2bb24304365e47933296d4dfd8a4960cbc8c4f819b3f241a131f07\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCcJZA\"}"}